    patch: version the fleet ops backup-heuristic fix — board DDL is not a project datastore, and a backup artifact is matched by basename. Addresses CF-370.
    
    `~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py` is tracked in no commit (CF-241), so this repo is
    the fix's only versioned home: `patches/fleet-ops-backup-heuristic.patch` against the
    pristine build sha256 82a3bf34…f81d976, plus `patches/fleet-ops-backup-heuristic.test.py`
    (argv[1] = target script, default the live path).
    
    Two defects in `ops_gaps()`, one phantom P1 class each:
    
    1. `owns_store` matched `schema.sql` as a path component anywhere under the root, so
       `.coding-hermes/board/schema.sql` (the foreman board's own DDL) and
       `.gitreins/state.db` counted as project datastores. 15 of the 26 flagged families
       fired only on those files, and the canonical board is git-tracked JSONL.
    2. The backup arm matched whole path COMPONENTS only (`backup`/`restore`/`snapshot`),
       so `docs/backup-set.md`, `docs/runbooks/backup-restore.md` and
       `scripts/backup-db.sh` were invisible and 10 more families were told their backup
       path did not exist.
    
    Measured on the live script, same host, same scheduler DB:
    
    - before: `fleet_ops_check.py --json` -> 26 families carry `check=backup`
      (scratch census-before.json)
    - after, patched build live: 7 families carry it (census-after.json). 19 cleared, 0 newly
      flagged — the fix only removes false positives, it never invents findings.
    - the 15 harness-triggered families report 0 backup gaps; bunker, consensus and eduos
      (the three named in AC2) are among the 19 cleared by the basename arm.
    - the 7 that still report carry no backup/restore doc or script at any depth <= 4
      (`find` over each workdir: crier, helios-work, heading, off-by-one, asce,
      dexdat/dexdat-core, plus HEADING as the same tree as heading). Those are genuine
      leads for their own -ops lanes, not the phantom class — the check is still alive.
    
    Negative controls (AC3, AC4), asserted in the test rather than described:
    migrations/001.sql with no backup-named artifact still reports P1; a real store
    (`data.db` / `store.db` / `state.db`) beside `.coding-hermes/board/schema.sql` still
    reports P1, so the harness exclusion cannot swallow a genuine datastore.
    
    Arms measured this tick: the test FAILS 24 arms on the pristine build and PASSES all 32
    on the patched build; `git apply --check` succeeds forward on a pristine copy (and the
    result is byte-identical to the patched live file, sha256 77d1deb2…6cd7829);
    `git apply --check --reverse` succeeds against the live patched file.
    
    Guard position, disclosed: the diff is a patch file plus a Python test — no `*.sh`
    touches, so the Tier 1 lint arm has nothing to grade and the guard refuses it exactly
    as CF-031 documents. The gate for this content is `bash tests/selftest.sh` at the
    landed tip plus the gitreins Tier 1 battery on the CF-370 task.
    
